# Theme & Palette Rules

Based on [VS Code Color Theme API](https://code.visualstudio.com/api/extension-guides/color-theme): workbench `colors` + TextMate `tokenColors`. Ether derives both from palette tokens — never patch generated theme JSON.

## Adding or editing a palette

Create/edit `src/palettes/ether-{name}.js`:

```js
export default {
  id: "ether-{name}",       // matches filename stem
  label: "Ether {Name}",
  type: "dark",               // "dark" | "light"
  uiTheme: "vs-dark",         // "vs-dark" | "vs"
  ui: { accent, fgPrimary, surfaceEditor, /* … */ },
  syntax: { default, comment, string, keyword, /* role keys */ },
};
```

Copy an existing palette as a template. All `ui` and `syntax` keys are validated at build time.

## Workbench derivation (required path)

1. **New workbench key** → add to `src/workbench/core-catalog.js` OR `extension-catalog.js`.
2. **Derive the value** in `derive-core.js` (core) or `derive-extensions.js` (chat/agent, menus, tabs).
3. Never emit keys from `DEPRECATED_THEME_COLOR_IDS` in `color.js`.
4. Keys in `TRANSPARENT_WORKBENCH_COLOR_IDS` must use alpha via `withAlphaByte` (not opaque `#RRGGBB`).

Use `mixColors`, `withAlphaByte`, `lighten`/`darken` from `src/utils/color.js` — not ad-hoc hex math.

## Syntax highlighting

- Rules live in `src/syntax/rules.js` — one shared set across all 20 themes.
- Map scopes to `syntax.{role}` tokens (`comment`, `keyword`, `function`, etc.).
- `SYNTAX_RULE_COUNT` must equal `EXPECTED_SYNTAX_RULE_COUNT`; tests enforce this.
- **Do not** add `semanticTokenColors` or `settings.background` on token rules.

## Contrast & validation

Build fails if palette tokens miss WCAG targets in `PALETTE_CONTRAST_TARGETS` (`fgPrimary`, `fgMuted`, `syntax.default`, `syntax.comment`, `fgOnAccent`). Tune base tokens, not generated output.

## Removing a theme

Delete the palette file and run `npm run build` — orphaned JSON and `package.json` entries are cleaned automatically.
